Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/043-v2-default-model-and-follow-ups (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)

THE DECISION (from the operator, 2026-10-21): cli-opencode now has a per-version default model.
- OpenCode 1: `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at `--variant max` (unchanged). Form: `opencode run --model opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash --variant max ...`.
- OpenCode 2: `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at `#max` (DevPass, LLM Gateway). Form: `opencode2 run --standalone -m llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max ...`. Reason: OpenCode 2 lists no `opencode-go` provider unless it is logged in to it separately (`opencode2 providers login opencode-go`), so the v1 default fails on a typical v2 install, while `llmgateway` is listed.

HOW TO APPLY IT:
1. Every OpenCode 2 dispatch example that shows the DEFAULT dispatch and today reads `-m opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash#<level>` becomes `-m llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash#<level>`. Keep the level as written.
2. Do NOT change OpenCode 1 forms (`--model opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`, `--variant ...`). They keep opencode-go.
3. Do NOT change text that describes the opencode-go route itself rather than the default dispatch, for example a roster row about `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` saying what its v2 form is. There, keep `-m opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max` and add, once per such row, that v2 needs its own opencode-go login.
4. Prose that says what the default is must state both versions. Never say the default is the same on both versions.
5. A v2 pre-flight or provider check for the default now checks the `llmgateway/` prefix, not `opencode-go/`.
Before editing, list every line in your files that contains `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` (rg -n), classify each as v1-form, v2-default-dispatch, route-description or prose-default, and edit only the last three as above.

TASK: apply the decision to the cli-opencode playbook and prompt templates listed under ALLOWED WRITE PATHS. Scenario files that compare providers or variants on purpose (for example `multi-provider/variant-levels-comparison.md`) keep any v2 opencode-go line that is part of the comparison, and say that it needs a v2 opencode-go login. Do not change any dated record (a line that starts with `Coverage note (`), and do not edit anything under `changelog/` or `benchmark/`.

